[00:20.54]1. When the eyes of blind ones see again
[00:26.97]And the ears of deaf ones hear again,
[00:33.17]When the songs of children fill the air
[00:40.17]And joy and peace are ev’rywhere,
[00:46.67]When our loved ones will return to life,
[00:55.25]To an earth that’s free from sin and strife,
[01:03.83](Chorus)
[01:12.41]You will see how God these things supplies,
[01:20.99]If you keep your eyes on the prize.
[01:29.56]2. When the wolves and lambs will feed as one,
[01:35.56]When the bears and calves bask in the sun,
[01:42.56]Then a mere young boy will lead them all,
[01:52.12]And they will heed his childish call.
[01:57.12]When our tears belong to yesterday,
[02:02.12]When our fears and pain have passed away,
[02:05.62](Chorus)
[02:09.12]You will see how God these things supplies,
[02:23.71]If you keep your eyes on the prize.